Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-18-2001||10:28 AM||||FieroGTracer... did you use my light-lens method (<A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010073.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010073.html</A>)?  Looks like you have amber colored reflectors on the top?  ...or is that just the reflection from the bulbs?  looks cool!  How'd it go?  I have one set ready, but I'm waiting on LEDs still...  I've had quite a request for these too (especially after taking my sample to fierorama-).  I'd like to make a buck from wood & bondo to be able to produce them a little more quickly & precisely.  Glad to see someone else running with the idea!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierogtracer||09-18-2001||07:35 PM||||Just the reflection and got those LEDs in the Brake and Parking lights. Had to modify the 3rd brake light it causes a dead ground when not lit. And led are not designed like a 2 filament bulb so they would not work like the others.<P>The only differece from mine and yours is I used a Satin finish clear paint to coat inside.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_11.jpg"> ||||reg||1
